// Our garden and our mini forest, shared so we both tend the same things.
// The garden: sixteen plots in raised beds. Plant a seed in each pot, water it once
// (the can holds six, the well refills it), pull the weeds (they feed the compost,
// which makes fertiliser), and it grows from a seed to a bloom; now and then one
// blooms golden. Picked flowers go in the vase on our table and onto the shelves,
// one pot per kind, and the gnome wishes for a different flower every day.
// The forest: ten spots round a pond to grow trees in, some of them fruit trees
// that fill the basket, with a fairy ring, fireflies, ducklings and a hedgehog.
